        ":question/worked-solution": "The horizontal asymptote of $y={2}^{x}$ is $y=0.$ The vertical translation $y={2}^{x}+c$ shifts the asymptote to $y=c.$\n\nIn the graph above, the horizontal asymptote is $y=-3.$ Therefore, $c=-3.$"
